WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.630 --> 00:00:02.280
- A mother and son found dead,

00:00:02.280 --> 00:00:04.350
millions of dollars in missing money,

00:00:04.350 --> 00:00:06.930
and the downfall of a family dynasty.

00:00:06.930 --> 00:00:08.670
The saga of the Murdaugh Family

00:00:08.670 --> 00:00:10.200
attracted national attention,

00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:13.320
after disbarred South Carolina
Lawyer, Alex Murdaugh,

00:00:13.320 --> 00:00:15.810
was accused of killing his wife and son.

00:00:15.810 --> 00:00:19.020
- Every day, almost, since the homicides

00:00:19.020 --> 00:00:20.190
something new has happened,

00:00:20.190 --> 00:00:22.500
and I think that's just
captivating to people.

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:23.460
- [Elise] Murdaugh was charged

00:00:23.460 --> 00:00:26.520
with two counts of murder in July 2022,

00:00:26.520 --> 00:00:28.800
after his wife Maggie and son Paul,

00:00:28.800 --> 00:00:30.870
were found fatally shot a year earlier

00:00:30.870 --> 00:00:32.760
at the family's hunting estate.

00:00:32.760 --> 00:00:34.860
He's pleaded not guilty to the charges

00:00:34.860 --> 00:00:38.280
and will face trial in Colleton
County, South Carolina.

00:00:38.280 --> 00:00:39.510
Here's what you need to know

00:00:39.510 --> 00:00:42.210
about the case against Alex Murdaugh.

00:00:42.210 --> 00:00:44.790
The first stage of the
trial is jury selection,

00:00:44.790 --> 00:00:46.710
but because of the prominent family name

00:00:46.710 --> 00:00:48.060
selecting 12 jurors

00:00:48.060 --> 00:00:50.820
that aren't familiar with the
Murdaugh Family or the case

00:00:50.820 --> 00:00:52.320
will be a challenge.

00:00:52.320 --> 00:00:54.690
- Jury selection is just
gonna be incredibly tough,

00:00:54.690 --> 00:00:55.980
everybody knows the Murdaugh's.

00:00:55.980 --> 00:00:57.390
- [Elise] That's because the legacy

00:00:57.390 --> 00:00:59.400
and legal influence of the Murdaugh Family

00:00:59.400 --> 00:01:01.140
in Southeastern, South Carolina,

00:01:01.140 --> 00:01:03.930
dates back to the early 1900s.

00:01:03.930 --> 00:01:04.980
The family established

00:01:04.980 --> 00:01:07.770
one of the state's
dominant law firms in 1910,

00:01:07.770 --> 00:01:09.480
and three generations of Murdaugh's

00:01:09.480 --> 00:01:12.780
have presided as solicitors
over the 14th Judicial Circuit,

00:01:12.780 --> 00:01:15.310
which covers five
counties in South Carolina

00:01:16.200 --> 00:01:18.000
- From, you know, 1920,

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:20.490
when the first Murdaugh ran for office,

00:01:20.490 --> 00:01:22.770
until, you know, 2006,

00:01:22.770 --> 00:01:25.710
they knew every law enforcement
officer in their region.

00:01:25.710 --> 00:01:26.790
- [Elise] The local agencies

00:01:26.790 --> 00:01:28.380
that first arrived at the crime scene

00:01:28.380 --> 00:01:30.090
recused themselves from the case

00:01:30.090 --> 00:01:33.000
because of the family's close
ties to law enforcement.

00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:34.950
- They have this pretty
serious reputation,

00:01:34.950 --> 00:01:37.230
even now, even with Alex Murdaugh in jail

00:01:37.230 --> 00:01:38.850
for more than a year,

00:01:38.850 --> 00:01:41.850
people are still
intimidated by this family

00:01:41.850 --> 00:01:43.890
because they've known
him their whole life.

00:01:43.890 --> 00:01:46.920
- Richard Alex Murdaugh,
are you guilty or not guilty

00:01:46.920 --> 00:01:49.945
of the felonies wherein
you stand indicted?

00:01:49.945 --> 00:01:50.880
- Not Guilty.

00:01:50.880 --> 00:01:52.770
- [Elise] While investigating
the double homicide,

00:01:52.770 --> 00:01:54.630
law enforcement discovered evidence

00:01:54.630 --> 00:01:57.150
of a string of alleged financial crimes.

00:01:57.150 --> 00:01:58.860
- He was a personal injury lawyer.

00:01:58.860 --> 00:02:01.800
His clients were some of
the poorest of the poor

00:02:01.800 --> 00:02:03.420
and the most badly injured,

00:02:03.420 --> 00:02:07.170
and he's accused of siphoning
money off of judgements

00:02:07.170 --> 00:02:09.600
that he won on behalf of his clients.

00:02:09.600 --> 00:02:11.190
- [Elise] Murdaugh has pleaded not guilty

00:02:11.190 --> 00:02:13.080
to most of those charges.

00:02:13.080 --> 00:02:14.940
But in a filing submitted to the court,

00:02:14.940 --> 00:02:17.220
prosecutors state, "The alleged wrongdoing

00:02:17.220 --> 00:02:20.610
that led to these charges
gave him motive for murder."

00:02:20.610 --> 00:02:22.710
- Alex was under a huge amount of pressure

00:02:22.710 --> 00:02:25.980
to turn over to the court
evidence of his finances

00:02:25.980 --> 00:02:28.350
in a boat crash case involving his son.

00:02:28.350 --> 00:02:30.570
And prosecutors say that
if he had done that,

00:02:30.570 --> 00:02:32.190
it would've led to the unraveling

00:02:32.190 --> 00:02:34.320
of this alleged scheme of crime

00:02:34.320 --> 00:02:35.790
that he'd been running for a decade,

00:02:35.790 --> 00:02:40.020
and that was enough to
set him off that night

00:02:40.020 --> 00:02:41.520
and kill his wife and son.

00:02:41.520 --> 00:02:42.630
- [Elise] Prosecutors state that,

00:02:42.630 --> 00:02:44.460
After Maggie and Paul were found dead,

00:02:44.460 --> 00:02:46.410
people immediately treated Defendant

00:02:46.410 --> 00:02:49.050
as the victim of an unspeakable tragedy.

00:02:49.050 --> 00:02:51.210
The day of reckoning vanished."

00:02:51.210 --> 00:02:52.747
The defense has called this theory,

00:02:52.747 --> 00:02:55.350
"Illogical and implausible."

00:02:55.350 --> 00:02:57.450
- The prosecution has a tough climb here.

00:02:57.450 --> 00:02:59.670
They have got to prove
beyond a reasonable doubt

00:02:59.670 --> 00:03:01.770
that Alex alone committed these murders,

00:03:01.770 --> 00:03:04.080
in a circumstantial case, and in a case

00:03:04.080 --> 00:03:07.320
where the evidence is in
some question in some cases.

00:03:07.320 --> 00:03:08.520
- [Elise] The shirt Murdaugh wore

00:03:08.520 --> 00:03:09.660
on the night of the murders

00:03:09.660 --> 00:03:13.080
is expected to be a key piece
of evidence in the trial.

00:03:13.080 --> 00:03:14.490
According to court documents,

00:03:14.490 --> 00:03:17.070
'It had microscopic
amounts of blood spatter."

00:03:17.070 --> 00:03:18.367
Something prosecutors say,

00:03:18.367 --> 00:03:21.120
"Indicates Murdaugh was close
to one of his family members

00:03:21.120 --> 00:03:22.380
when they were shot."

00:03:22.380 --> 00:03:24.847
But in a separate filing,
defense attorneys claimed that,

00:03:24.847 --> 00:03:28.140
"The state used unreliable
methods to test the shirt,

00:03:28.140 --> 00:03:31.470
ultimately making it
impossible to test further."

00:03:31.470 --> 00:03:33.960
- It could help the
prosecution if their expert

00:03:33.960 --> 00:03:34.793
is able to say,

00:03:34.793 --> 00:03:38.580
"Yes, there was this this
high-velocity impact spatter

00:03:38.580 --> 00:03:39.450
on the shirt."

00:03:39.450 --> 00:03:41.790
But it opens up a chance for the defense

00:03:41.790 --> 00:03:42.690
'cause they were never able

00:03:42.690 --> 00:03:45.840
to have their own expert
independently look at it.

00:03:45.840 --> 00:03:47.580
- [Elise] Instead, the
prosecution could lean

00:03:47.580 --> 00:03:50.310
on digital evidence to
help prove their case.

00:03:50.310 --> 00:03:52.230
Court documents filed by the defense

00:03:52.230 --> 00:03:54.967
describe a video recorded
on Paul's phone saying,

00:03:54.967 --> 00:03:57.810
"He can be heard having a
lighthearted conversation

00:03:57.810 --> 00:03:59.820
with his mom and dad in the background,

00:03:59.820 --> 00:04:01.890
which places Murdaugh
at the hunting estate

00:04:01.890 --> 00:04:04.890
a little over an hour
before he called 911,

00:04:04.890 --> 00:04:07.890
which conflicts with the
timing of his alibi."

00:04:07.890 --> 00:04:09.487
- The defense has said,

00:04:09.487 --> 00:04:11.520
"Yeah, maybe he was imprecise about,

00:04:11.520 --> 00:04:13.080
you know, who we saw and when.

00:04:13.080 --> 00:04:15.870
But what that video shows is them laughing

00:04:15.870 --> 00:04:17.430
and talking with one another.

00:04:17.430 --> 00:04:18.900
So this was a loving family,

00:04:18.900 --> 00:04:20.250
and you're gonna tell me that

00:04:20.250 --> 00:04:21.780
after this video was recorded,

00:04:21.780 --> 00:04:24.807
Alex Murdaugh shot his wife
and kid, that's unacceptable."

00:04:26.160 --> 00:04:28.710
- [Elise] The trial is
expected to last several weeks

00:04:28.710 --> 00:04:32.160
and prosecutors are seeking
life imprisonment for Murdaugh.

00:04:32.160 --> 00:04:33.600
- It's incredible to think about,

00:04:33.600 --> 00:04:36.900
the family built this
name for a hundred years,

00:04:36.900 --> 00:04:39.000
and the reason it will be remembered

00:04:39.000 --> 00:04:42.791
is because of Alex and what
he's alleged to have done.

00:04:42.791 --> 00:04:45.541
(dramatic music)

